@page "/privacy"
@model Site.Pages.PrivacyModel
<div class="container narrow">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
        Document Number Validator is a documentation and demo site for an open-source .NET library.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
        With your consent, this site uses Google Analytics (Google tag, measurement ID
        <code>G-972WK5CM96</code>) to understand how the site is used — for example, which pages are visited
        and how visitors arrive. Google Analytics sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_gid</code>)
        and collects data including your IP address, browser and device information, and the pages you view.
        This data is processed by Google and may be transferred to and stored on servers outside your country.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>The Google tag only loads after you click “Accept”.</strong> If you decline, or never respond,
        no analytics cookies are set and no analytics data is collected. No advertising or marketing trackers
        are used.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can change or withdraw your choice at any time via the “Cookie settings” link in the footer, or
        opt out of Google Analytics with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser
        Add-on</a> or your browser's tracking-protection settings. See the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> for details.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
        The only first-party browser storage used is your colour-theme preference and your analytics choice
        (<code>localStorage</code>), which never leave your device. The analytics cookies described above are
        set by Google Analytics only after you accept.
    </p>

    <h2>Demo inputs</h2>
    <p>
        Values you enter in the on-page demo are processed in memory on the server for the current request
        so that validation can run. They are not persisted, logged to the application data store or shared
        with third parties. Do not enter real personal or financial data into the demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
        As with any hosted website, the hosting provider may keep standard infrastructure logs (such as IP
        address, requested URL and timestamp) for security and operations purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
        The website source and the validator libraries are public on
        <a href="@SiteInfo.WebsiteRepositoryUrl" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. If you have questions or want to
        request a change, open an issue.
    </p>
</div>
